{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1xMAR5mb9wyhJQZmNB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish failed because `similarity()` returned a Python `float`, and DynamoDB rejects floats. I've fixed it and added a regression test. Nothing was deployed or published, and nothing was committed.\n\n**Cause:** The first publish works only because the table is empty, so `similar` is `[]`. The second publish finds one existing story, so `similar` gets `{\"slug\": ..., \"score\": <float>}`. boto3 raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, which isn't a `ValueError`, so `handler()` returns a 500. The existing test only publishes into an empty table, so it never hit this path.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `src/app.py`: `similarity()` now returns `Decimal(str(round(...)))`, so the stored score is a `Decimal`.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: new `test_second_publish_stores_related_scores` publishes two stories through `handler()` and checks for a 201, the expected `similar` entry, and a `Decimal` score. It fails on the old code and passes with the fix.\n\n**Why it won't come back:** `tests/fake_dynamo.py` already rejects floats the way boto3 does, and the new test exercises the non-empty `similar` path. The full suite passes (2 tests). No stored data needs repair, since the failed writes stored nothing.\n\nThe explanation and fix are in `ANSWER.md`. The changes are uncommitted in the working tree."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1120,"cache_read_input_tokens":30690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1120},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3fa7514-82bb-481f-96d8-e54adf1f599f","uuid":"f6415e2d-aa50-4cf